  "identity": {
    "playing_style": "Under İsmail Kartal (appointed June 2026 on a one-year deal, his fourth spell) Turkish media report a 4-3-3 as the main plan with 4-2-3-1 as the alternative used in some pre-season games, and Kartal publicly demanded a 'pressing' game before the season opener at Gençlerbirliği. Squad construction points to a senior, experienced core (Ederson, Škriniar, Aké, Guendouzi, Asensio, Lukaku, Greenwood) built to win domestic duels and compete in Europe rather than a young transition team.",
    "principles": [
      "title-now imperative (no league title since 2013/14)",
      "experienced-star recruitment",
      "domestic-legend coaching appointments",
      "heavy reliance on loan returns and squad churn",
      "10+4 foreign-player rule shapes squad building"
    ],
    "club_character": "Member-owned association with one of Turkey's largest fanbases; extremely high pressure and volatile governance — three presidents in twelve months (Ali Koç -> Sadettin Saran, elected 21 Sep 2025 -> Aziz Yıldırım, elected 7 Jun 2026 with 17,245 votes vs 9,927 for Hakan Safi, on record turnout of 27,000+). Coaches and sporting directors are changed quickly: Domenico Tedesco and sporting director Devin Özek were dismissed on 27 Apr 2026, a day after a 0-3 derby defeat at Galatasaray ended the title race. Intense Istanbul media environment.",
    "ownership": "member-owned sports club (association); president elected by congress members",
    "political_and_social_context": "Publicly documented institution-level facts only: (1) leadership instability with an extraordinary elective congress in June 2026, only nine months after the September 2025 election; the new president serves one year because bylaws require a regular election in May/June 2027. (2) Club debt was reported cut from ~EUR 600m (2018) to ~EUR 307m (mid-2024) under the previous administration; the 2026 presidential candidates campaigned on large transfer-spending promises. (3) Management publicly aimed to offload high earners (e.g. Talisca, EUR 7.5m net) to fund signings in summer 2026. (4) Long-running institutional rivalry/antagonism with Galatasaray and with the TFF over refereeing is a recurring public theme.",
    "languages": [
      "tr",
      "en",
      "pt",
      "es"
    ],
    "wage_structure": "hierarchical (several high earners; Talisca reported at EUR 7.5m net before leaving)",
    "transfer_policy": "star-driven, short-term; mixes free/expiring senior signings (Aké, Lukaku, Muriqi, Greenwood) with sales of saleable foreigners (Oosterwolde, Archie Brown targeted for ~EUR 25m / 15m) to satisfy the 10+4 foreign-player limit and wage budget",
